<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="2d981900-084f-579e-80c8-aeb426ad0e48" activityNameId="a841eeac-8d89-5e84-972f-8c38ba2492b9" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transport, aircraft, freight, short-haul, Betrieb</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transport, aircraft, freight, short-haul, Betrieb
Inventory refers to the entire transport life cycle. Airport infrastructure expenditures and environmental interventions are accounted for using the yearly transport performance at uniqueairport in Zurich (478'800 tkm/a). Aircraft manufacturing is allocated based on the total life span of an aircraft (50'000 LTO) , the average distance of a flight (750km) and its transport performance (0.84t/unit);
UUID: 58b89551-b63f-3b44-9556-9c44605b8f8b
The dataset describes the operation of aircrafts including taxying, take-off and landing covering fuel consumption and operation emissions. Aircraft manufacture and maintenance, airport construction, operation and dismantling are inputs to this dataset
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Aircraft operation modelled based on passenger aircrafts operated by Lufthansa Group in 2019. The emission profiles distinguish between LTO and cruise.
Time period: Start date refers to emission factor data. End date refers to year of reporting fuel consumption and transport activities
Production volume: 325'000'000 tkm
Sampling: fuel consumption is based on corporate data, emission profiles are based on FOEN statistics 
Extrapolations: Allocation between passengers and freight based on weight (average passenger weight between 158kg and 163kg); allocation between booking classes based on seat area.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_58b89551-b63f-3b44-9556-9c44605b8f8b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">RER</shortname>
        <comment>
